 36S  c  2008Sp01: E=70 MeV {+36}S beam was provided from the Cologne           
 36S 2c  accelerator facility. The multi-layer target was 0.19 mg/cm{+2} natural
 36S 3c  C, 3.03 mg/cm{+2} Gd, 1.0 mg/cm{+2} Ta, and 2.0 mg/cm{+2} Cu. The Gd   
 36S 4c  layer was cooled to liquid-nitrogen temperature and magnetized to      
 36S 5c  saturation by a 0.06-T external field. Forward-scattered {+12}C ions   
 36S 6c  from Coulomb excitation and |a particles from {+8}Be produced via the  
 36S 7c  |a-transfer reaction 12C(36S,8Be)40Ar were detected by a 300-mm{+2} Si 
 36S 8c  counter at 0|'. |g rays were measured by four 12.7|*12.7-cm NaI(Tl)    
 36S 9c  scintillators at 65|' and 115|' and by a 40% Ge detector at 0|'.       
 36S Ac  Measured E|g, I|g, particle-|g coin, Counting Rate Double Ratio, and   
 36S Bc  particle-|g Angular Correlation Slope. Deduced Precession Angles and g 
 36S Cc  factors, lifetimes from DSAM lineshape analysis. Calculated B(E2)|^    
 36S Dc  from their measured lifetimes. Compared with OXBASH shell-model        
 36S Ec  calculations using the WBT interaction in the sdfp space.              
